尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的直接生理浓度测量值，也未提供基于直接TME测量的疗效相关性数据。P0582研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅报告了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高血浆肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗后的更长总生存期相关（中位OS：高水平组33个月 vs. 低水平组22个月），并指出ICB治疗后血浆肌苷水平下降。该研究未进行人体肿瘤组织内的直接定量，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。P0589研究利用患者来源异种移植（PDX）小鼠模型结合微透析技术，证实了在人源肿瘤组织中可检测到肌苷且存在瘤内差异，但未报告具体的绝对浓度数值，也未涉及ICI疗效的相关性分析。P0588综述提及一般文献中血浆肌苷为低微摩尔级，而坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔级，但这属于引用的一般性背景陈述，并非本研究对特定人体TME的实测数据。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内”的具体浓度及其与ICI疗效的直接量化关联，当前材料缺失核心实证数据。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels prior to or during ICB treatment：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1) and human RCC patients / Plasma inosine levels decreased after ICB treatment compared to baseline/pre-treatment states / During/after ICB therapy：Post-ICB (Mice & Humans): Reduced levels (qualitative)\\nGeneral physiological context (cited literature) / Concentration ranges: Blood plasma low micromolar; Necrotic/hypoxic TME hundreds of micromolar / General physiological conditions：Blood plasma: Low micromolar range；Necrotic/Hypoxic TME: Hundreds of micromolar range\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告内源性肌苷水平与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效之间的具体相关性统计。目前证据主要局限于以下层面：1. 临床队列关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，较高的基线血浆肌苷水平与接受纳武利尤单抗治疗后的更长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但这是血浆数据而非肿瘤组织/间质液数据，且未提供具体的浓度数值（如 μM 或 ng/mL）。2. 机制与药代动力学背景：肌苷可直接抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素激活酶 UBA6，增强肿瘤免疫原性；其在血浆中的半衰期约为 15 小时，而腺苷降解极快。体外及小鼠模型显示，在葡萄糖受限条件下，效应 T 细胞可利用肌苷作为替代碳源支持增殖和功能，且在肿瘤细胞无法利用肌苷的模型中，外源性补充肌苷可增强 ICI 疗效。3. 方法学可行性：基质辅助激光解吸电离质谱成像（MALDI-MSI）和微透析技术已被证明可在人类非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）组织和患者来源异种移植（PDX）模型中检测肌苷等代谢物，但相关研究未结合 ICI 治疗结果进行定量关联分析。4. 干预性试验：一项 II 期临床试验显示，外源性补充肌苷联合 PD-1/PD-L1 抑制剂可延长晚期实体瘤患者的无进展生存期（HR 0.63），但这属于外源性干预效果，不能直接反映内源性 TME 肌苷浓度的自然变异及其与疗效的剂量-反应关系。综上，缺乏针对人体肿瘤局部（组织或间质液）肌苷浓度的直接定量测量及其与 ICI 响应（ORR/PFS/OS）的统计学关联数据。\\n\\n[[\\\"这项研究在 CheckMate 025 临床试验的肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中分析了血浆代谢组数据，发现基线血浆肌苷水平较高与总生存期（OS）延长显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。\\\", \\\"研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。\\\", \\\"作者明确指出由于样本完整性问题（intact samples missing），未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测或验证肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。\\\", \\\"研究揭示了肌苷增强 ICB 疗效的分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。\\\"], [\\\"该综述详细阐述了肌苷（inosine）作为肠道微生物代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的三大分子机制：(1) 特异性抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素样修饰激活酶 6（UBA6）活性，提高肿瘤免疫原性；(2) 结合 T 淋巴细胞上的腺苷 A2A 受体，激活 cAMP-CREB 信号级联，促进 Th1 细胞分化及肿瘤浸润；(3) 在葡萄糖受限的肿瘤微环境（TME）中作为替代能源底物维持效应 T 细胞的生存和细胞毒性功能。\\\", \\\"文中指出肌苷由特定肠道菌群（如假长双歧杆菌 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum、约氏乳杆菌 Lactobacillus johnsonii 等）合成，并在免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗破坏肠道屏障完整性后易位至体循环，从而激活抗肿瘤 T 细胞。\\\", \\\"综述提及了临床转化潜力，指出在存在肌苷代谢缺陷的实体瘤中，外源性肌苷补充可能恢复免疫细胞代谢适应性，从而增强 ICI 疗效，这为理解肌苷浓度与疗效的关系提供了理论框架。\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（口服 400 mg/kg）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\\\", \\\"体外实验中使用了 100 μM 的肌苷浓度处理肿瘤细胞以观察 UBA6 抑制效果，但这并非人体内源性浓度的实测数据。\\\", \\\"研究指出肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"], [\\\"综述提供了“肠道微生物群 - 代谢物 - 免疫轴”的整体概念框架，解释了代谢物如何作为分子信使从肠腔易位至体循环并调节全身及局部抗肿瘤免疫。\\\", \\\"文中还总结了其他核心代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节免疫的具体机制及在不同肿瘤类型（如食管癌、胃癌、肝癌、结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌）中的微生物特征签名，为理解肌苷在整体代谢网络中的位置提供了背景。\\\", \\\"讨论了针对微生物组的干预策略（如 FMT、益生菌、工程菌）在增强 ICI 疗效方面的转化潜力和当前面临的标准化、安全性及监管挑战。\\\"]]\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          \"人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性\",\n          \"CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值\"\n        ],\n        \"limits\": [\n          \"需要寻找直接在人体肿瘤组织活检、间质液或微透析样本中测定肌苷绝对浓度（μM/ng/mL）的研究，并确认这些浓度数据是否与接受 ICI 治疗的患者的临床结局（如 ORR、PFS、OS）存在显著的相关性或因果联系。\"\n        ],\n        \"still_missing\": \"该研究未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据（如 μM 或 ng/mL），也未报告 TME 内肌苷浓度与 ICI 疗效（如 ORR、PFS 或 OS）的直接定量统计关联。虽然提供了血浆肌苷水平与生存期的相关性以及肿瘤组织 UBA6 表达与缓解率的相关性，但作者明确承认由于样本缺失，未在人类肿瘤组织中直接测量肌苷浓度，因此核心的'TME 内肌苷具体浓度阈值’及‘组织层面浓度 - 疗效直接挂钩’的证据在此材料中缺失。\",\n        \"allowed_use\": [\n          \"background_context\",\n          \"explicit_objectives\",\n          \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n          \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n          \"explicit_leads\"\n        ],\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:220699268\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\n            \"year\": \"2020\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:220699268\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\n            \"year\": \"2020\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:280543786\",\n            \"title\": \"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:291235137\",\n            \"title\": \"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286562058\",\n            \"title\": \"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"7f1c43ec9ba638ccffb6291e9f21c1e1b48f6fc6\",\n            \"title\": \"Multifaceted role of inosine in complex diseases and human health.\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1093/nutrit/nuae029\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0599\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0580\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"c5e74d5eebf19335caebc97bdb8300261fcb0ee5\",\n            \"title\": \"Targeting ribosomes reprograms the tumour microenvironment and augments cancer immunotherapy\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41416-025-03109-y\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0579\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"1e76d13192f1c1a75fec92c6e6a2de5934fc6a1f\",\n            \"title\": \"Characterisation of an autochthonous mouse ccRCC model of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy resistance\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-04917-1\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0581\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\n            \"title\": \"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0639\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:259947308\",\n            \"title\": \"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\n            \"year\": \"2023\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0634\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n            \"year\": \"2023\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:280543786\",\n            \"title\": \"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0634\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n            \"year\": \"2023\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286562058\",\n            \"title\": \"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0581\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\n            \"title\": \"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0639\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:259947308\",\n            \"title\": \"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\n            \"year\": \"2023\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:219269178\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\n            \"year\": \"2019\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\n            \"title\": \"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers18010034\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:272644866\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1002/cam4.70143\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:219269178\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\n            \"year\": \"2019\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:280543786\",\n            \"title\": \"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"CorpusId:280543786\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"unresolved_identity\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286644045\",\n            \"title\": \"Single-cell-based identification of drug synergy with immunotherapy via tumor microenvironment remodeling\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2025-014132\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\n            \"title\": \"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers18010034\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0581\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\n            \"title\": \"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:272644866\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1002/cam4.70143\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:220699268\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\n            \"year\": \"2020\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:219269178\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\n            \"year\": \"2019\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\n            \"title\": \"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers18010034\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:291235137\",\n            \"title\": \"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0589\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W4296038319\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0586\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\n            \"title\": \"Dual-function engineered bacteria remodel AML tumor microenvironment via IL-12 delivery and adenosine depletion to sustain NK cell immunity\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1182/blood-2025-5912\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\n            \"title\": \"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers18010034\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:272644866\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:272644866\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1002/cam4.70143\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0591\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:291487342\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:291487342\",\n            \"title\": \"Peripheral blood biomarkers in PD-1/PD-L1 immunotherapy: distinguishing predictive from prognostic biomarkers\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1924506\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0592\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"3720efcbdc55365f98b0da676548b3d1debd5944\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"3720efcbdc55365f98b0da676548b3d1debd5944\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract B046: Sensitizing the PDAC tumor microenvironment to immune checkpoint therapies: characterization of a PDAC 3D model to decipher immune infiltration\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.pancreatic24-b046\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286644045\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286644045\",\n            \"title\": \"Single-cell-based identification of drug synergy with immunotherapy via tumor microenvironment remodeling\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2025-014132\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286927958\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286927958\",\n            \"title\": \"Targeting the gut microbiota-metabolite-immune axis in cancer immunotherapy: mechanistic interplay, therapeutic strategies, and translational applications-a narrative review\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.21037/tcr-2025-1992\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"c3ad940c5555f03c559b2198cb68aace35fa7dba\",\n            \"canonical_paper_id\": \"c3ad940c5555f03c559b2198cb68aace35fa7dba\",\n            \"title\": \"Abstract 2033: Rigosertib promotes anti-tumor activity of cancer cells via CETSA revealed novel targets and activates NLRP3-dependent inflammatory responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2024\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2024-2033\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"unresolved_identity\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"question\": \"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\n        \"usable_content\": \"现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体统计关联。P0582 研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅检测了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高基线血浆肌苷与尼莫鲁单抗治疗后的较长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs. 22个月），但明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；该研究还指出肌苷在血浆中半衰期较长（约15小时），但未提供具体的血浆或组织浓度数值。P0588 研究主要关注体外 T 细胞代谢及小鼠模型，虽提及血液血浆中肌苷浓度为低微摩尔范围、坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据，且明确指出缺乏人类临床相关性数据。P0587 综述同样未提取具体浓度值，仅引用其他研究关于粪便短链脂肪酸或精氨酸的数据示例。因此，当前材料无法回答人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的具体浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的相关性问题。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未见其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效（如ORR、PFS或OS）的具体统计关联结果。多项研究指出这是当前文献中的关键缺失环节：尽管有临床观察显示接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平较高与总生存期延长相关（中位OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但研究者承认由于样本完整性问题，未能在其22人的临床队列中直接测量肌苷，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标；另有综述和机制研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非针对接受ICI治疗的人类患者的实测数据。此外，虽然有小鼠模型证实口服肌苷可增强ICB疗效，且体外实验显示T细胞可利用肌苷作为碳源，但这些前临床数据无法直接外推为人体内的具体浓度阈值或疗效相关性。目前缺乏将人源肿瘤组织或间质液中的肌苷定量值与ICI响应直接挂钩的证据。\\n\\n[\\\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏将肌苷等代谢物在粪便、血液、肿瘤组织及间质液中的配对定量测量与临床结局关联的证据。具体而言：P0582 报告了肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平与生存期的关联（高肌苷组中位总生存期33个月 vs 低肌苷组22个月），但明确说明未在人肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度，仅以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理指标；P0588 指出虽然理论推测坏死/缺氧微环境中肌苷可达数百微摩尔，但该研究本身未在人类患者中测量TME内的肌苷浓度，且其引用的数值为外部文献的一般性陈述而非本研究数据；P0587 和 P0589 均强调，尽管有微生物产生肌苷增强小鼠ICI疗效的机制证据，但缺乏人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷浓度的直接定量数据，且现有的SCFA数据多局限于粪便样本，未链接至TME浓度或ICI结果。因此，关于人体TME内肌苷的具体浓度阈值及其对ORR/PFS/OS的统计关联，当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究确认了腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将腺苷（Ado）转化为肌苷（Ino）的酶动力学参数（Km=0.05, Vmax=53µmol/min），并在体外实验中证实了腺苷暴露会抑制免疫细胞杀伤力，而转化为肌苷可恢复免疫功能。研究提及使用 LC-MS 评估 ADA 动力学和活性，表明肌苷及相关代谢物在实验体系中是可测量的。这为肌苷在肿瘤微环境中具有免疫刺激作用而非抑制作用提供了机制性证据，支持了微环境代谢重编程可能影响免疫治疗效果的假设。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究对象为工程化非致病性大肠杆菌（E. coli K12 DH5α），通过表面展示 IL-12 和 ADA 融合蛋白发挥作用。体内实验主要在免疫 competent 的 B16-F10 黑色素瘤小鼠模型和 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型中进行，观察到细菌在骨髓和肿瘤部位的聚集。免疫效应主要评估了 NK 细胞的活化标志物（CD25, NKp30）及细胞因子（IFNγ, TNFα），未直接报告 T 细胞检查点抑制剂（ICI）的使用或响应数据。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据。研究P0582仅报告了人体血浆（血清）中肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效的关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，基线血浆肌苷水平较高者接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的中位总生存期为33个月，显著高于低水平组的22个月。该研究明确指出，由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中直接验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。此外，P0582提到腺苷降解为肌苷的半衰期差异（约15小时），暗示了检测策略的挑战，但未给出具体的人体组织浓度数值。其他材料如P0588和P0596主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，其中P0588引用文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这并非本研究在人体中的实测数据；P0596提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸浓度，而非人体内源性肌苷浓度。P0639虽然建立了尿液中肌苷的定量方法并报告了膀胱癌患者术前术后尿液浓度的变化（术后24小时升高约1.7倍），但尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          \"人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性\",\n          \"CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值\"\n        ],\n        \"limits\": [\n          \"需要找到直接在人体肿瘤组织活检、间质液或微透析液中测量肌苷绝对浓度，并将其与ICI治疗响应（如ORR、PFS、OS）进行统计关联的研究。目前的证据仅限于血浆水平的间接关联或动物模型/体外实验。\"\n        ],\n        \"still_missing\": \"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\n        \"allowed_use\": [\n          \"background_context\",\n          \"explicit_objectives\",\n          \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n          \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n          \"explicit_leads\"\n        ],\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:220699268\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\n            \"year\": \"2020\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:220699268\",\n            \"title\": \"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\n            \"year\": \"2020\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:280543786\",\n            \"title\": \"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\n            \"year\": \"2025\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\n            \"original_source_handle\": \"P0587\",\n            \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n            \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n            \"year\": \"2022\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:291235137\",\n            \"title\": \"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\n            \"year\": \"2026\",\n            \"doi\": \"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\n            \"original_sourc